IMPORT prelude
IMPORT daydate
IMPORT `je21-nouns`

-- je21-seat-defaults: the reading of each fork that the exported questions use.
-- Each fork L1 to L11 is a place where the text supports two readings that give different answers (NOTES.md section 6).
-- The exported questions take no reading as an input: they use the default named here.
-- The other reading of each fork is reached by calling the rule module's function with that reading, which the rule modules' tests do.
-- The first constructor of each fork's enumeration is its default.

§ `Defaults for the forks`

GIVETH A `Reading L1 of the day after a silent provision is made`
`default reading L1` MEANS `the Law does not say at what time of that day, so a question about a time of day on it is refused`

GIVETH A `Reading L2 of a stated time of day`
`default reading L2` MEANS `a stated time of day is provision to the contrary, and the legislation comes into force at that time`

GIVETH A `Reading L3 of the time at which the Law came into force`
`default reading L3` MEANS `the beginning of 28 September 2021, by Article 3(2)`

GIVETH A `Reading L4 of the day on which a Law was made`
`default reading L4` MEANS `the day it was registered, by Article 2(4)`

GIVETH A `Reading L5 of legislation made by the States`
`default reading L5` MEANS `made by the States means adopted by the States Assembly, as Article 2(1)(a) and 2(3)(a) put it, so it covers Laws, Regulations and Acts`

GIVETH A `Reading L6 of the limits in Article 9(6)`
`default reading L6` MEANS `the limits bear on provision that amends other legislation, and incidental provision of any other kind is not limited by them`

GIVETH A `Reading L7 of Article 11(4)`
`default reading L7` MEANS `the 3 sittings run from the commencement of Part 2, which is what paragraph (4) says`

GIVETH A `Reading L8 of Article 2(2)`
`default reading L8` MEANS `the declaration by Act of the States is all that Article 2(2) requires`

GIVETH A `Reading L9 of Article 5 and legislation that expires`
`default reading L9` MEANS `Article 5 applies to legislation that has expired or otherwise ceased to have effect, whether or not other legislation repealed it`

GIVETH A `Reading L10 of Article 5(3) where provision is made to the contrary`
`default reading L10` MEANS `a contrary provision that displaces paragraph (2) displaces paragraph (3) too, which speaks only of things mentioned in paragraph (2)`

GIVETH A `Reading L11 of whether Article 17(2) is the only route to an official version of consolidated legislation`
`default reading L11` MEANS `Article 17(2) is the only route, so consolidated legislation that does not meet it is not an official version`
